questions.prompt_en:
Implement `count_chars(text)` that counts how many times each character appears in the string `text`. Return a dict mapping each character to its count. An empty string returns an empty dict `{}`.

Examples:
```python
count_chars('hello')  # -> {'h': 1, 'e': 1, 'l': 2, 'o': 1}
count_chars('aaa')    # -> {'a': 3}
count_chars('')       # -> {}
```

questions.solution:
def count_chars(text):
    counter = {}
    for ch in text:
        counter[ch] = counter.get(ch, 0) + 1
    return counter

questions.tests:
assert count_chars('hello') == {'h': 1, 'e': 1, 'l': 2, 'o': 1}
assert count_chars('aaa') == {'a': 3}
assert count_chars('') == {}
assert count_chars('ab ab') == {'a': 2, 'b': 2, ' ': 1}
assert count_chars('AaAa') == {'A': 2, 'a': 2}

